# No Sensitive Data in Code or Tests

This project is open source. **Never** commit or hardcode:

- **Credentials**: API usernames, passwords, API keys, Bearer tokens, OAuth secrets
- **Real account data**: Real FastSpring company IDs, order references, subscription IDs from production or staging
- **Personal data**: Real email addresses, names, or customer identifiers (except obviously fake examples)

## Allowed

- **Environment variables**: Read secrets from `process.env` or `.env` (e.g. `FS_API_USERNAME`, `FS_API_PASSWORD`, `MCP_API_KEYS`). Document required vars in `.env.example` only.
- **Test fixtures**: Obviously fake values only, e.g. `"test-user"`, `"test-pass"`, `"a@b.com"`, `"key-alpha-0000..."`, `"VI8201014-6538-11102S"` (example format), synthetic IDs like `"sub-sbl-1"`, `"ord-modern-1"`.
- **Comments/docs**: Refer to env var names (e.g. "Set FS_API_USERNAME in .env"); never paste real values.

## Integration tests

- Use **only** values from environment (e.g. `process.env.TEST_ORDER_REFERENCE`, `process.env.TEST_SUBSCRIPTION_ID`). Skip or fail clearly if required env is missing.
- Do not fall back to hardcoded "golden" IDs or credentials.

## If you need a secret in code

- Add it to `.env` (gitignored) and reference it via config/env. Add a placeholder to `.env.example` with a short comment.
